# WALK_IS_VALUES -- 1 rows. dsl.py:334-335 walks `_fields` and looks the value up BY NAME, so the FIELD list's order and spelling are the encoding. dsl.bend's raw_walk walks the VALUE list (its `Vf` carries the field), so the value list's order and spelling are. `raw_ord_swap` transposes the ORDER: two fields at the same bits with different names, so the LAST write wins and the field order decides the word.
raw_ord_swap	|0x00000016	|0x0000000b

# MODMASK -- 16 rows. THE TAUTOLOGY IS FIXED: `src_bit.vdst` was `String.eq("vdst","vdst")` -- a
# literal compared with itself, so it took bit 8 for EVERY name and `sdst`/`op`/`nosuch` all answered
# 8 where CPython answers 0. It now reads `String.eq(name, "vdst")`, the single-name arm of
# dsl.py:313-321, and those three pins are DROPPED rather than moved. The remaining 16 are the OTHER
# half of this class, which is untouched: `mod_mask` never tests WHICH modifier is set, so neg/abs/opsel
# come out equal.
